    <string name="privacy_policy_content">Privacy Policy\n\nDocvra is a PDF and document utility designed to process your documents locally on your device.\n\nLocal Document Processing\n\nDocuments, PDFs, images, text, filenames, and document contents selected or created in Docvra are processed locally on your device. Docvra does not intentionally upload your documents or their contents to our servers.\n\nFile Access\n\nDocvra uses Android\'s Storage Access Framework to let you select files and choose where generated files are saved. The app does not request broad access to all files on your device.\n\nCamera\n\nDocvra may request access to your device camera when you use document-scanning features. Camera images captured for document processing are handled locally by the app and are not intentionally sent to our servers.\n\nAdvertising\n\nDocvra uses Google AdMob to display advertisements, including native, interstitial, and app-open advertisements.\n\nThe Google Mobile Ads SDK may automatically collect and process information such as IP address, interactions with ads or the app, diagnostic information, and device or account identifiers where applicable. Google may use this information for purposes including advertising, measurement, analytics, and fraud prevention.\n\nDocvra does not intentionally provide the Google Mobile Ads SDK with the contents of your PDFs, documents, scanned pages, filenames, document text, or Storage Access Framework document URIs.\n\nConsent and Privacy Choices\n\nDocvra uses Google\'s User Messaging Platform (UMP) to manage privacy and advertising consent choices where required. Depending on your region and applicable requirements, you may be presented with privacy choices relating to advertising and data processing.\n\nWhere required, privacy options may also be made available so that you can review or change applicable choices.\n\nPush Notifications\n\nDocvra uses Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM) to provide push notifications.\n\nFirebase Cloud Messaging and related Firebase installation services may process technical information required to provide notifications, such as the application version, Firebase-related technical information, and a per-installation Firebase identifier.\n\nDocvra may subscribe the app installation to notification topics so that notifications can be delivered to groups of installations.\n\nSome notifications may contain links to Google Play. If you choose to tap such a notification, Docvra may open the corresponding Google Play destination.\n\nDocvra does not intentionally send your PDF contents, document contents, filenames, document text, scanned pages, or document URIs to Firebase Cloud Messaging.\n\nAnalytics and Crash Reporting\n\nDocvra does not include Firebase Analytics or Firebase Crashlytics as direct application dependencies. Advertising services may nevertheless process measurement, interaction, and diagnostic information as described in the Advertising section above.\n\nInternet Access\n\nInternet access is used for functions that require network communication, including advertising, consent/privacy messaging, and push notifications. Core document processing remains local to the device.\n\nThird-Party Services\n\nDocvra uses services provided by Google, including Google AdMob, the User Messaging Platform, and Firebase Cloud Messaging. Information processed by these services is also subject to Google\'s applicable privacy policies and service terms.\n\nYour Choices\n\nYou can control notification permission through Android system settings. You can also manage certain advertising and privacy choices when those options are made available through the consent/privacy interface.\n\nChanges to This Privacy Policy\n\nThis Privacy Policy may be updated when Docvra\'s features, third-party services, or applicable requirements change. The current version will be made available through the app or the application\'s published privacy-policy location.</string>
